CORE
main.py
--unwind 5

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
convert_with now emits the __exit__(self, None, None, None) call after
the with-body (in reverse order of entry), so an assertion/bug inside
__exit__ is checked. Previously __exit__ was never invoked (differential
unsoundness witness 4). Now detected; promoted to CORE. (Exception
suppression -- a __exit__ returning True clearing an active exception --
is not yet modeled; only the normal-exit cleanup path.)
